tion rather than a fixed-window sum.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Signal efficiency at the allocated rate must be at least 80%.\",\n      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n      \"evidence\": \"No signal-efficiency simulation results are available in the provided documents. The recommendation is the most plausible latency-compliant choice, but the 80% efficiency requirement cannot be directly verified from the available evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Algorithm latency on Level-1 FPGA hardware must not exceed 4.0 us.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"firmware_testbench_results.md gives Algorithm-L3 latency as 3.1 us, below the 4.0 us Level-1 latency budget. Algorithm-L1 is 5.8 us and therefore excluded; Algorithm-L2 is 1.9 us but is less sophisticated.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Threshold between 20 and 60 GeV.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The recommended threshold is 40 GeV, which lies within the allowed 20--60 GeV range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Finish by submitting one recommended algorithm and threshold.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Submitted a single recommendation: Algorithm-L3 with a 40 GeV threshold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Allocated trigger rate is 8 kHz.\",\n      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n      \"evidence\": \"rate_allocation.md states the signature is allocated 8 kHz, but no rate-vs-threshold data are provided to prove that Algorithm-L3 at 40 GeV exactly meets this rate.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}", "call_id": "call_a34452d6b83b4d58937ab4dfe1ec9719", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_097a0f7a3974d370006b02de14e2fc87d09b8d6db8ca2022c5", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
